ing constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly available to everyone.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e70\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay minimum-revenue guarantees on GPU capacity in exchange for a share of revenue above the guaranteed level.\", \"passages\": [\"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity. In exchange for this backstop, Nvidia also shares in a portion of the Neocloud’s revenue earned above the backstop level.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started backstopping Neoclouds’ data-center leases.\", \"passages\": [\"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop program typically runs for six years, with Nvidia ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis models an illustrative Nvidia backstop price averaging $2.36 over six years, which it considers near the low end of the range, and expects most Neoclouds to negotiate higher backstops.\", \"passages\": [\"The below table is an illustrative example to explain the basic terms of the program – we present a backstop pricing curve that we believe to be on the lower end of the backstop range – in this case at an average of $2.36 over the six-year period, but we expect that most Neoclouds will negotiate higher backstops.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\", \"summary\": \"SharonAI’s June 2026 Australia AI-factory deal includes a six-year backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs valued at $4.88 billion; SharonAI plans a 132 MW footprint, 102 MW contracted, and more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027.\", \"passages\": [\"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\", \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360 MW AI cluster in Batam, Indonesia, with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; it is likely to be housed at a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\", \"passages\": [\"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\", \"summary\": \"Firmus expects $25 billion to $30 billion of customer revenue over six years from its project; SemiAnalysis expects Firmus to share some revenue above the backstop level with Nvidia.\", \"passages\": [\"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\", \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 600 MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will underwrite 1.2 GW of renewable development and 1.5 GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032.\", \"passages\": [\"Beyond this – Firmus also announced a 600MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will also underwrite 1.2GW of new renewables development and 1.5GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says other Neoclouds have Nvidia backstops, although many have not been publicly disclosed.\", \"passages\": [\"We have seen many other neoclouds having backstops, but many are not public yet.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis estimates initial lending for Nvidia-backstopped Neocloud projects will price wider than five-year hyperscale-backed deals at about SOFR plus 225 basis points and 5.9% yield, but tighter than CoreWeave’s five-year unsecured bonds at about 10% yield.\", \"passages\": [\"We think that initial lending will be at a wider spread than the current 5y backstopped hyperscale deals which come in at around SOFR + 225bps (roughly equivalent to a Z-spread of 195bps, or about 5.9% total yield) but at a tighter spread than CoreWeave’s 5-year unsecured corporate bond which has a yield of ~10% (roughly equivalent to Z-spread of 600bps).\"]}]}\n{\"point\": 12, \"decisive_item\": {\"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\", \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\", \"status\": \"claim\", \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"}}, \"kept_from_that_article\": [{\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e67\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says market estimates for Nvidia shipment volumes and revenue in the second half of 2026 are materially below its supply-chain-tracking estimates.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e68\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital spending will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028 and cumulative spending will reach about $11.1 trillion over 2024–2029, with credit markets the main funding source.\", \"passages\": [\"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028. Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e69\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says data-center supply improved by early 2026, chip production became the limiting constraint, and financing was a significant obstacle to expanding compute by mid-2026.\", \"passages\": [\"In 2025, we wrote extensively about how datacenter capacity was the bottleneck for AI compute growth. By early 2026, the datacenter supply situation improved considerably, but it became clear that chip production was now the limiting constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly available to everyone.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e70\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay minimum-revenue guarantees on GPU capacity in exchange for a share of revenue above the guaranteed level.\", \"passages\": [\"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity. In exchange for this backstop, Nvidia also shares in a portion of the Neocloud’s revenue earned above the backstop level.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started backstopping Neoclouds’ data-center leases.\", \"passages\": [\"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop program typically runs for six years, with Nvidia ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis models an illustrative Nvidia backstop price averaging $2.36 over six years, which it considers near the low end of the range, and expects most Neoclouds to negotiate higher backstops.\", \"passages\": [\"The below table is an illustrative example to explain the basic terms of the program – we present a backstop pricing curve that we believe to be on the lower end of the backstop range – in this case at an average of $2.36 over the six-year period, but we expect that most Neoclouds will negotiate higher backstops.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\", \"summary\": \"SharonAI’s June 2026 Australia AI-factory deal includes a six-year backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs valued at $4.88 billion; SharonAI plans a 132 MW footprint, 102 MW contracted, and more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027.\", \"passages\": [\"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\", \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360 MW AI cluster in Batam, Indonesia, with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; it is likely to be housed at a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\", \"passages\": [\"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\", \"summary\": \"Firmus expects $25 billion to $30 billion of customer revenue over six years from its project; SemiAnalysis expects Firmus to share some revenue above the backstop level with Nvidia.\", \"passages\": [\"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\", \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 600 MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will underwrite 1.2 GW of renewable development and 1.5 GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032.\", \"passages\": [\"Beyond this – Firmus also announced a 600MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will also underwrite 1.2GW of new renewables development and 1.5GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says other Neoclouds have Nvidia backstops, although many have not been publicly disclosed.\", \"passages\": [\"We have seen many other neoclouds having backstops, but many are not public yet.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis estimates initial lending for Nvidia-backstopped Neocloud projects will price wider than five-year hyperscale-backed deals at about SOFR plus 225 basis points and 5.9% yield, but tighter than CoreWeave’s five-year unsecured bonds at about 10% yield.\", \"passages\": [\"We think that initial lending will be at a wider spread than the current 5y backstopped hyperscale deals which come in at around SOFR + 225bps (roughly equivalent to a Z-spread of 195bps, or about 5.9% total yield) but at a tighter spread than CoreWeave’s 5-year unsecured corporate bond which has a yield of ~10% (roughly equivalent to Z-spread of 600bps).\"]}]}\n{\"point\": 13, \"decisive_item\": {\"day\": \"2026-07-01\", \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\", \"who\": \"The Information (prior reporting)\", \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\", \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\", \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\", \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\", \"status\": \"rumour\"}}, \"kept_from_that_article\": [{\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e2\", \"summary\": \"The Information reported on 2026-07-01 that NVIDIA would repurchase participating young cloud providers’ unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price if they could not secure enough customers.\", \"passages\": [\"On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e3\", \"summary\": \"The Information reported that NVIDIA’s program includes declining revenue-share rates over contract terms and that Firmus and Sharon AI had joined it, with three executives confirming the arrangement.\", \"passages\": [\"In return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract. GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e4\", \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced on 2026-07-01 a business model combining revenue sharing and credit support for AI cloud providers procuring its infrastructure.\", \"passages\": [\"On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e5\", \"summary\": \"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs; Firmus is constructing a Batam campus planned to reach up to 360 MW and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\", \"passages\": [\"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e6\", \"summary\": \"NVIDIA’s May 2026 regulatory filing disclosed that it had added $3.5 billion of guarantees for customer data-center leases in exchange for rights to purchase the customers’ shares.\", \"passages\": [\"According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e7\", \"summary\": \"The Information reported that NVIDIA was negotiating to guarantee OpenAI’s lease of a large Ohio data center, whose fully built-out cost could reach $500 billion.\", \"passages\": [\"According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\"]}]}\n{\"point\": 14, \"decisive_item\": {\"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (post on Monday)\", \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\", \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\", \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\", \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, \"kept_from_that_article\": [{\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e52\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture is delayed to 2028 because of midplane manufacturability challenges.\", \"passages\": [\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e53\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis said Nvidia’s NVL576 system is likely to be delayed or limited to small volumes.\", \"passages\": [\"NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e54\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis said Nvidia scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud service providers and hyperscalers objected to its design and operating burden.\", \"passages\": [\"A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e55\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis said Nvidia has no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size, potentially giving AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\", \"passages\": [\"That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e56\", \"summary\": \"Nvidia said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e57\", \"summary\": \"Nvidia’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e58\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis projected Nvidia data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\", \"passages\": [\"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\"]}]}\n{\"point\": 15, \"decisive_item\": {\"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\", \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (as reported)\", \"passage\": \"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled; two-die version remains\", \"how_much\": \"roughly half the real-world compute\", \"status\": \"claim\", \"status_note\": \"cancelled\"}}, \"kept_from_that_article\": [{\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e129\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 AI server rack has been delayed more than 12 months to 2028 because its PCB midplane is difficult to manufacture without defects.\", \"passages\": [\"Asian tech stocks slid after analyst firm SemiAnalysis reported on X that Nvidia's next AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems. The issue, according to SemiAnalysis, is the circuit boards. Specifically, the PCB midplane, a central board that connects all the individual components, has proven extremely difficult to produce without defects.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e130\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia scrapped its planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, after cloud providers and large data center operators objected to its form factor and operational overhead.\", \"passages\": [\"A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely. Cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e131\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"passages\": [\"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e132\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, two generations from the current one.\", \"passages\": [\"A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e133\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to offset the product shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\"]}]}\n{\"point\": 16, \"decisive_item\": {\"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\", \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (as reported)\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis, about NVIDIA's plan\", \"what\": \"sell more Oberon-Rubin racks to cover the Kyber gap\", \"status\": \"plan\", \"status_note\": \"as claimed\"}}, \"kept_from_that_article\": [{\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e129\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 AI server rack has been delayed more than 12 months to 2028 because its PCB midplane is difficult to manufacture without defects.\", \"passages\": [\"Asian tech stocks slid after analyst firm SemiAnalysis reported on X that Nvidia's next AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems. The issue, according to SemiAnalysis, is the circuit boards. Specifically, the PCB midplane, a central board that connects all the individual components, has proven extremely difficult to produce without defects.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e130\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia scrapped its planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, after cloud providers and large data center operators objected to its form factor and operational overhead.\", \"passages\": [\"A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely. Cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e131\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving only the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"passages\": [\"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e132\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, two generations from the current one.\", \"passages\": [\"A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\"]}, {\"ref\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e133\", \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to offset the product shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"passages\": [\"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-trace/trace-packet-r4.json\\\")); x=p[11]; print(json.dumps(x[\\\"decisive_item\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)); [print(i[\\\"ref\\\"],i[\\\"summary\\\"],i[\\\"passages\\\"]) for i in x[\\\"kept_from_that_article\\\"]]' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-trace/trace-packet-r4.json\\\")); x=p[11]; print(json.dumps(x[\\\"decisive_item\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)); [print(i[\\\"ref\\\"],i[\\\"summary\\\"],i[\\\"passages\\\"]) for i in x[\\\"kept_from_that_article\\\"]]' \"","aggregated_output":"{\"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\", \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\", \"status\": \"claim\", \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"}}\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e67 SemiAnalysis says market estimates for Nvidia shipment volumes and revenue in the second half of 2026 are materially below its supply-chain-tracking estimates. ['Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e68 SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital spending will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028 and cumulative spending will reach about $11.1 trillion over 2024–2029, with credit markets the main funding source. ['Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028. Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e69 SemiAnalysis says data-center supply improved by early 2026, chip production became the limiting constraint, and financing was a significant obstacle to expanding compute by mid-2026. ['In 2025, we wrote extensively about how datacenter capacity was the bottleneck for AI compute growth. By early 2026, the datacenter supply situation improved considerably, but it became clear that chip production was now the limiting constraint. Now – mid-way through the year – it is clear that financing will now be one of the most significant obstacles to ramping large scale compute broadly available to everyone.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e70 SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay minimum-revenue guarantees on GPU capacity in exchange for a share of revenue above the guaranteed level. ['This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity. In exchange for this backstop, Nvidia also shares in a portion of the Neocloud’s revenue earned above the backstop level.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71 SemiAnalysis reports that Nvidia has started backstopping Neoclouds’ data-center leases. ['Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72 SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop program typically runs for six years, with Nvidia ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term. ['Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73 SemiAnalysis models an illustrative Nvidia backstop price averaging $2.36 over six years, which it considers near the low end of the range, and expects most Neoclouds to negotiate higher backstops. ['The below table is an illustrative example to explain the basic terms of the program – we present a backstop pricing curve that we believe to be on the lower end of the backstop range – in this case at an average of $2.36 over the six-year period, but we expect that most Neoclouds will negotiate higher backstops.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74 SharonAI’s June 2026 Australia AI-factory deal includes a six-year backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs valued at $4.88 billion; SharonAI plans a 132 MW footprint, 102 MW contracted, and more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027. ['The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75 Firmus announced a 360 MW AI cluster in Batam, Indonesia, with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; it is likely to be housed at a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park. ['Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76 Firmus expects $25 billion to $30 billion of customer revenue over six years from its project; SemiAnalysis expects Firmus to share some revenue above the backstop level with Nvidia. ['Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77 Firmus announced a 600 MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will underwrite 1.2 GW of renewable development and 1.5 GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032. ['Beyond this – Firmus also announced a 600MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will also underwrite 1.2GW of new renewables development and 1.5GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78 SemiAnalysis says other Neoclouds have Nvidia backstops, although many have not been publicly disclosed. ['We have seen many other neoclouds having backstops, but many are not public yet.']\ngnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79 SemiAnalysis estimates initial lending for Nvidia-backstopped Neocloud projects will price wider than five-year hyperscale-backed deals at about SOFR plus 225 basis points and 5.9% yield, but tighter than CoreWeave’s five-year unsecured bonds at about 10% yield. ['We think that initial lending will be at a wider spread than the current 5y backstopped hyperscale deals which come in at around SOFR + 225bps (roughly equivalent to a Z-spread of 195bps, or about 5.9% total yield) but at a tighter spread than CoreWeave’s 5-year unsecured corporate bond which has a yield of ~10% (roughly equivalent to Z-spread of 600bps).']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"point\":1,\"extracted\":\"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e166\",\"why\":\"It says Micron expects tight memory-market conditions could last until 2028.\"}\n{\"point\":2,\"extracted\":\"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e167\",\"why\":\"It says new memory capacity will not come online until 2027 or later, leaving supply low.\"}\n{\"point\":3,\"extracted\":\"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e169\",\"why\":\"Its quoted passage states Micron expects $50 billion in revenue next quarter.\"}\n{\"point\":4,\"extracted\":\"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e104\",\"why\":\"It states Micron forecast an 86% adjusted gross margin next quarter.\"}\n{\"point\":5,\"extracted\":\"gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c#e198\",\"why\":\"It reports China's plan to let top AI companies buy limited quantities of H200 chips.\"}\n{\"point\":6,\"extracted\":\"none\",\"why\":\"The kept item does not say Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy H200 chips.\"}\n{\"point\":7,\"extracted\":\"none\",\"why\":\"The kept item does not say domestic AI-chip suppliers were sold out or buyers were considering weaker chips.\"}\n{\"point\":8,\"extracted\":\"none\",\"why\":\"The kept item does not state that Trump allowed H200 exports to select customers in December 2025.\"}\n{\"point\":9,\"extracted\":\"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\"why\":\"It states Sharon disclosed a $4.88 billion backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs over six years.\"}\n{\"point\":10,\"extracted\":\"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\"why\":\"It states Firmus announced a 360 MW Batam cluster with an Nvidia backstop.\"}\n{\"point\":11,\"extracted\":\"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\"why\":\"It states Firmus expected $25 billion to $30 billion in customer revenue over six years.\"}\n{\"point\":12,\"extracted\":\"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\"why\":\"It states that other neoclouds have Nvidia backstops that are not public, though it does not state the negotiations or accelerating announcements.\"}\n{\"point\":13,\"extracted\":\"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e7\",\"why\":\"It states Nvidia was negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of an Ohio data center.\"}\n{\"point\":14,\"extracted\":\"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e52\",\"why\":\"It states Kyber NVL144 was reported delayed to 2028 because of midplane manufacturing challenges.\"}\n{\"point\":15,\"extracted\":\"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e131\",\"why\":\"It states the four-die Rubin Ultra was cancelled and the remaining two-die version delivers roughly half the performance.\"}\n{\"point\":16,\"extracted\":\"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96#e133\",\"why\":\"It states Nvidia planned to offset the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks.\"}\n{\"point\":17,\"extracted\":\"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587#e56\",\"why\":\"It states Nvidia rejected the report and said its roadmap remained intact.\"}\n{\"point\":18,\"extracted\":\"gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571#e149\",\"why\":\"It quotes the Nvidia representative saying the roadmap was intact.\"}\n{\"point\":19,\"extracted\":\"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e6\",\"why\":\"It states Nvidia added $3.5 billion in customer data-center lease guarantees in exchange for rights to buy shares.\"}\n{\"point\":20,\"extracted\":\"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\"why\":\"It states Nvidia had started backstopping neocloud data-center leases.\"}"}}
